<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a storage conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A storage conveyor holds product in a controlled queue between line sections, sized to ride through long stops such as changeovers and shift breaks. Types include vertical spirals, serpentine loops, multi-tier tables, and mass-flow tables. Storage conveyors prevent upstream shutdowns during downstream stops.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is the difference between FIFO and LIFO?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>FIFO releases products in entry order, first in, first out. LIFO releases the most recently stored product first. FIFO is required for <a href="/industries/food-conveyors/">food</a>, pharmaceutical, and any product with expiration dates or lot tracking. In-line spirals and serpentine loops run FIFO. Off-line spirals that reverse to return product run LIFO.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">How much buffer does a packaging line need?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Buffer capacity should cover the longest typical downstream stop. Use the formula: Products/min x Stop Duration (min) x Product Pitch (ft) = Storage Length. A 30 CPM line needing 10 minutes of buffer at 18-inch pitch requires 450 feet, achievable in a compact spiral or serpentine layout.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What are the main types of storage conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Four types: vertical accumulation spirals (compact, FIFO), horizontal serpentine loops (bottles/cans, FIFO), multi-tier storage tables (highest capacity, complex controls), and mass-flow accumulation tables (beverage lines, partial FIFO). Choose based on product type, capacity needed, floor space, and FIFO requirements.</p>

</div>
